  "summary": "New preprints tailor pretraining to clades, methylation and ncRNA, test why personal-genome fine-tuning stalls, and design tissue-specific enhancers.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is DNA and RNA sequence foundation models moving from generic pretraining toward specialized inputs, diagnostic probing, and design. Several preprints narrow scope or enrich inputs. An apicomplexan model pretrained on 455 assemblies improves regulatory-signal prediction in data-sparse Plasmodium falciparum. ModBERT adds population variants and long-read CpG methylation. B-RANKO applies a 150M-parameter bidirectional decoder-only architecture to ncRNA. MARRI encodes opening penalties and hybridization gains for RNA-RNA interaction prediction. Other work examines what these models capture. Region-aware pooling over 5' UTR, CDS and 3' UTR outperforms global mean pooling in linear probes. LAMP attributes the failure of personal-genome fine-tuning to improve expression prediction to distal effects. Fine-tuned Borzoi and AlphaGenome perform comparably to, not better than, variant-based methods in admixed Latino whole blood. On design, GENECraft couples a genomic language model with a functional oracle without training. REGAL uses reinforcement learning over regulatory grammar to produce tissue-specific enhancers, validated across species.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-20"
}
